Package: caagro
Type: Package
Title: Applied Statistics for Agricultural Experimentation with 'shiny' Interfaces
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Wilhan", "Valasco dos Santos",
           email = "wilhanvalasco@hotmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A statistical analysis platform for agricultural and
    biological experimentation, usable through scriptable R functions or
    point-and-click 'shiny' applications that call the same functions.
    Provides data import and validation; analysis of variance for completely
    randomised, randomised complete block and factorial designs with type
    I, II or III sums of squares and estimated marginal means; multiple
    comparisons (Tukey-Kramer, Student-Newman-Keuls, Fisher's LSD,
    Scott-Knott, Dunnett, Games-Howell, Bonferroni and Holm) with compact
    letter displays (Piepho, 2004 <doi:10.1198/1061860043515>); residual
    diagnostics; t tests, Welch's ANOVA and planned contrasts; linear,
    polynomial, non-linear (exponential, logarithmic, power, logistic,
    Gompertz, Michaelis-Menten, Mitscherlich, log-logistic, linear-plateau)
    and binomial regression, with confidence and prediction bands, model
    comparison by information criteria (Akaike, 1974
    <doi:10.1109/TAC.1974.1100705>) and agronomic quantities such as maximum
    technical efficiency, economic optimum dose and effective dose;
    non-parametric tests (Kruskal-Wallis, Friedman, Mood's median, Dunn,
    Conover, Wilcoxon, sign and permutation tests); classical and bootstrap
    confidence intervals (Efron, 1987 <doi:10.1080/01621459.1987.10478410>);
    principal component analysis, hierarchical clustering, k-means and
    correlation matrices; and a common, fully customisable 'ggplot2'
    graphics editor with high-resolution export, 'Excel' workbooks,
    HTML reports and reproducible R scripts.
